---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
Astro.response.headers.set("Cache-Control", "public, max-age=86400");
---
<Base title="Terms of use — Cleburne Wire" desc="The ground rules for reading Cleburne Wire, sending tips and listing updates, and buying a sponsorship.">
  <header class="page-head"><h1>Terms of use</h1><p class="dek">The ground rules for using this site. Last updated September 30, 2026.</p></header>
  <div class="single">
    <h3 class="group">What the site is</h3>
    <p>Cleburne Wire is an independent local news and guide site. It is not affiliated with the City of Cleburne, any school district, or any local newspaper. News items are short summaries written with the help of software, and every story links to its original source. Read the source for the full account.</p>
    <h3 class="group">Accuracy and corrections</h3>
    <p>We work to get things right, but summaries, listings, event times, rates and other information can be incomplete or out of date. Don't rely on the site for emergencies, legal, medical or financial decisions. If something is wrong, tell us at <a href="mailto:news@cleburnewire.com">news@cleburnewire.com</a> and we'll correct it.</p>
    <h3 class="group">What you send us</h3>
    <p>When you send a tip, photo, event, or listing update, you confirm you have the right to share it and let us publish, edit and display it on the site and our social pages. Don't send anything unlawful, private about someone else, or that you don't own.</p>
    <h3 class="group">Business listings</h3>
    <p>The Guide lists local businesses from public information. Owners can update their own listing for free. Listing a business is not an endorsement.</p>
    <h3 class="group">Sponsorships</h3>
    <p>Sponsorships are month to month unless stated otherwise, and you can cancel from your Stripe receipt. Paid placements are always labeled. Sponsors never influence news coverage. We don't run political campaign ads, adult content, vaping or payday lending, and we may decline or remove any ad. Billing questions: <a href="mailto:news@cleburnewire.com">news@cleburnewire.com</a>.</p>
    <h3 class="group">Links to other sites</h3>
    <p>We link to many sources we don't control. Their content and policies are their own.</p>
    <h3 class="group">Changes</h3>
    <p>If these terms change, we'll update the date at the top of this page.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
